<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity down 0.3 pct in latest week.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity down 0.3 pct in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said on Monday liquidity in the banking system fell 0.3 percent, or 49 million sucres, to 15.85 billion sucres in the week to October 18.</p>
<p>At the end of September, bank liquidity stood at 15.35 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector at the end of 1995 was 12.51 billion sucres, up 41.2 percent from 1994.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
